{"version":"6.9","hitCount":209881,"nextCursorMark":"AoIIQGBAjSg1Njc0NTU4Ng==","nextPageUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=%28TITLE%3Aasthma+OR+ABSTRACT%3Aasthma%29&cursorMark=AoIIQGBAjSg1Njc0NTU4Ng%3D%3D&resultType=core&pageSize=50&format=json","request":{"queryString":"(TITLE:asthma OR ABSTRACT:asthma)","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"AoIIQGTPNig1NjU1MTc3Nw==","pageSize":50,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"43017212","source":"MED","pmid":"43017212","doi":"10.2147/ppa.s645459","title":"Mental Health Comorbidity and Health-Related Quality of Life Among U.S. Adults with Asthma: A Population-Based Cross-Sectional Study.","authorString":"Alwhaibi M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Alwhaibi M","lastName":"Alwhaibi","firstName":"Monira","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3707-0582"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Clinical Pharmacy, College of Pharmacy, King Saud University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3707-0582"}]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"20","journalIssueId":4091426,"dateOfPublication":"2026 ","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Patient Prefer Adherence","title":"Patient preference and adherence","essn":"1177-889X","issn":"1177-889X","nlmid":"101475748","isoabbreviation":"Patient Prefer Adherence"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-01-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"645459","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Depression and anxiety commonly coexist with asthma and may be associated with poorer health-related quality of life (HRQoL). This study examined their associations with HRQoL among US adults with asthma using nationally representative Medical Expenditure Panel Survey (MEPS) data.<h4>Methods</h4>A cross-sectional study was conducted using 2017-2022 data from the Medical Expenditure Panel Survey. Adults aged 18 years and older with asthma were categorized into four mutually exclusive groups: asthma only, asthma with depression, asthma with anxiety, and asthma with both depression and anxiety. HRQoL was assessed using the Veterans RAND 12-Item Health Survey (VR-12), which generates Physical Component Summary (PCS) and Mental Component Summary (MCS) scores. Multivariable linear regression analyses were performed to examine the associations between asthma groups and HRQoL after adjusting for the confounders while accounting for the complex survey design.<h4>Results</h4>The study included 5743 adults with asthma, of whom 68.4% had asthma alone, 10.2% had depression, 11.7% had anxiety, and 9.6% had both depression and anxiety. HRQoL differed significantly across the four groups (both p < 0.0001), with the highest PCS (44.04) and MCS (51.26) scores in the asthma-only group and the lowest scores (37.67 and 37.54, respectively) among those with both depression and anxiety. After adjustment for potential confounders, asthma with anxiety (β = -6.25, p < 0.001) and asthma with both depression and anxiety (β = -10.63, p < 0.001) and asthma and depression (β = -5.344, p < 0.001) were associated with lower MCS scores compared with asthma alone. Participants with both depression and anxiety also had significantly lower PCS scores (β = -0.85, p < 0.001).<h4>Conclusions</h4>Depression and anxiety were associated with poorer HRQoL among US adults with asthma, particularly mental HRQoL. Individuals with both conditions had the greatest impairment, highlighting the potential importance of incorporating mental health assessment into asthma care.","affiliation":"Department of Clinical Pharmacy, College of Pharmacy, King Saud University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Depression","Asthma","Anxiety","Mental health","Health-related Quality Of Life","Hrqol","Veterans Rand 12-Item Health Survey"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/PPA.S645459"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"N","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2026-11-12","dateOfCreation":"2026-11-12","dateOfRevision":"2026-11-12","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-11-07","firstPublicationDate":"2026-11-07","firstIndexDate":"2026-11-13","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42587790","source":"MED","pmid":"42587790","pmcid":"PMC13464759","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13464759"]},"doi":"10.3390/cells15151381","title":"Frequency of Local Allergic Asthma in Bronchial Asthma Patients: Role of Conjunctival Challenge and Neutrophil Histamine Release.","authorString":"López-Postigo A, Vega-Rioja A, Rodríguez-Neira C, Monteseirín J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"López-Postigo A","lastName":"López-Postigo","firstName":"Adrián","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7175-8789"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorio de Inmunología y Alergia-FISEVI, UGC de Alergología, Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."},{"affiliation":"Departamento de Medicina, Facultad de Medicina, Universidad de Sevilla, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."}]}},{"fullName":"Vega-Rioja A","lastName":"Vega-Rioja","firstName":"Antonio","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorio de Inmunología y Alergia-FISEVI, UGC de Alergología, Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."},{"affiliation":"Departamento de Medicina, Facultad de Medicina, Universidad de Sevilla, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."}]}},{"fullName":"Rodríguez-Neira C","lastName":"Rodríguez-Neira","firstName":"Claudia","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorio de Inmunología y Alergia-FISEVI, UGC de Alergología, Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."},{"affiliation":"Departamento de Medicina, Facultad de Medicina, Universidad de Sevilla, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."}]}},{"fullName":"Monteseirín J","lastName":"Monteseirín","firstName":"Javier","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorio de Inmunología y Alergia-FISEVI, UGC de Alergología, Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."},{"affiliation":"Departamento de Medicina, Facultad de Medicina, Universidad de Sevilla, 41009 Sevilla, Spain."},{"affiliation":"Hospital Quirón Sagrado Corazón, 41013 Sevilla, Spain."},{"affiliation":"Hospital Quirón Infanta Luisa, 41010 Sevilla, Spain."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7175-8789"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"15","volume":"15","journalIssueId":4243026,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Cells","title":"Cells","essn":"2073-4409","issn":"2073-4409","nlmid":"101600052","isoabbreviation":"Cells"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-07-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"1381","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>There is sufficient evidence to demonstrate the importance of local allergies in the various clinical conditions encompassed by allergic pathology. We sought to examine the frequency of Local Allergic Asthma (LAA) and to investigate whether neutrophils from patients with LAA were able to release histamine compared to neutrophils from patients with asthma diagnosed by skin prick test (SPT) and specific serum IgE (sIgE).<h4>Methods</h4>Sixty-eight patients with bronchial asthma and 15 healthy subjects were selected. All underwent SPT, and sIgE levels were determined. An allergen-specific conjunctival challenge (ASCC) and the allergen provocation test (APT) were carried out. Neutrophils were isolated, and their potential for histamine release was determined along with their influence on IgE receptors.<h4>Results</h4>Eighteen patients had a positive ASCC and a negative SPT and sIgE to certain allergens (52.9%), coexisting in 16 patients who were SPT and sIgE-positive to other allergens (CO-LOCAL ALLERGY); these were designated LOCAL ASTHMA A (LAA). Another group of 16 patients (47.1%) only had a positive ASCC (SENSITIZED) and were designated LOCAL ASTHMA B (LAB). The total number of patients who presented a local type of asthma was 34 (50%) (TOTAL LOCAL ASTHMA (TLA)). Neutrophils isolated from patients with local asthma were capable of releasing histamine, as were neutrophils from patients diagnosed by SPT and sIgE.<h4>Conclusions</h4>We have differentiated the clinical groups that may present LAA and have demonstrated how the neutrophils of these patients were capable of releasing histamine if stimulated with the allergen responsible for the clinical symptoms, with this release being IgE-dependent.","affiliation":"Laboratorio de Inmunología y Alergia-FISEVI, UGC de Alergología, Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena, 41009 Sevilla, Spain.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Conjunctiva","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Neutrophils","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N"